From 6cb2411933c7a4aafa2c0ed86107b631d583d97a
Subject: Add a Disabled depth of field mode that keeps the effect active
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/6cb2411933c7a4aafa2c0ed86107b631d583d97a
Date: 2026-10-13T12:08:04+01:00

No blur, but the component stays, so the transparent focus texture
is still rendered and the view key still asks transparent materials
to write it. Effects that read the focus target, such as the
explorer's star pass hiding stars behind imposters, keep working
when the user turns depth of field off. No pipelines are created,
so the node skips the view.
---
diff --git a/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/dof/mod.rs b/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/dof/mod.rs
index 11d9d6f0f82a5d7981b68cce14a520a13accbb97..b1ed472ec2ab524c25e80343a8ff91bd9da1d79b 100644
